// src/v4/std/report.dag
//
// Scope: advisory carrier — non-fail-closed information channel for programmer.
//        Distinct from std/diagnostic.dag's Diagnostic (which is fail-closed
//        per INVARIANTS P3 / C-8). Report is design-tier advisory output where
//        the programmer makes the choice. Used by lens/synthesis.dag (cross-
//        algorithm complexity) and any future advisory-tier lens.
// Anchor: docs/r4-carve-out-routing.md C7 design discrimination — "advisory
//         suggestions ... route through a separate introspection/report
//         carrier (NOT DiagnosticSeverity)"; INVARIANTS C-8 contrast (lens
//         enforcement is Error or it isn't — Report is the IS NOT branch)
//
// Owns:
//   - Report { reason: ReportReason, at: Locus, suggestion: ReportSuggestion }
//   - ReportReason (closed enum of advisory categories — DISJOINT from
//     Diagnostic's NamedReason; advisory-class vs error-class)
//   - ReportSuggestion (typed alternative the report points to; structurally
//     parallel to Diagnostic.suggested_correction but with non-blocking
//     semantics)
//
// Discipline:
//   - Report has NO Witness::Violates pairing. A lens emits Witness<Report>;
//     Holds means "no advisory observation," Violates means "advisory
//     observation present" — but Violates here is informational, not blocking
//   - Per opt-in-depth: a Report becomes blocking only via user-authored
//     apply_lens(<lens>, Enforce { ... }) declaration (THESIS:307-321)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/primitive.dag (String for messages)
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: Locus (shared structural reference for "where in
//     the program"; Report and Diagnostic share Locus but diverge on
//     reason/severity semantics)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-17
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.

module v4.std.report

